          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ध्वनति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ध्वनति — dhvanati — \"sounds; rings out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मन्दिरे शंखः ध्वनति। mandire śaṅkhaḥ dhvanati. A conch sounds in the temple."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): शंखः ध्वनितवान्, śaṅkhaḥ dhvanitavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ध्वनति (dhvanati) comes from the root √dhvan, \"to sound\", which also gives dhvani, \"a sound\"; KRM gives its participle dhvanita (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
