              "text": "दर्शनम् — darśanam — \"a sight of the deity; seeing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यात्रिकाः प्रातः मन्दिरे दर्शनं लभन्ते। yātrikāḥ prātaḥ mandire darśanaṃ labhante. In the morning the pilgrims are granted a sight of the deity in the temple."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दर्शनम् (darśanam) is built on the root √dṛś, \"to see\", with the ending -ana; MW gives darśana as seeing, sight and an audience, and the sight of a deity at a shrine is that sense in pilgrims' use (MW)."
